et"},{"type":"text","value":". The message type was never checked."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A mutation round on the state stack found it. The mutant that limited this\nbranch to updates (E3) survived the whole suite. With a strict mirror, the\noracle's histories showed 78 invalid updates on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":" and none under E3."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"repair-and-witnesses","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Repair and witnesses"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The oracle's mirror records each message that is invalid for its state, and\nevery history asserts that the list is empty. The deferred-sync lane already\ncompared exact per-key traces."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A previously absent key now always gets an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"insert"},{"type":"text","value":". When a buffered delete\nfor the key is still batched, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"composeBatchedChange"},{"type":"text","value":" turns the pair into an\nupdate, as before."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The completed-request map becomes a key set, the only part that\nvirtual-property derivation reads. The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" module is 194 minified and\n39 gzip bytes smaller."}]}]}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Owner on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"721a607e8"},{"type":"text","value":" (oracle only)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"26 of 378 fail, each on an update for a key the mirror lacks"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Owner on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"182b99262"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"378 pass"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutant: the old update branch"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the 26 failures above"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutant: no event for a previously absent key"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"92 of 538 owner tests fail"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"limits","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Limits"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The strict mirror runs in the change-event oracle's local-only histories.\nOther owners that build mirrors may still accept an update for an absent key."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Survivor: building the completed-key set empty changes no test result. The\nset only feeds the fallback for previous "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$synced"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$origin"},{"type":"text","value":" when the\npre-sync capture lacks the key. This repair keeps that use unchanged; the\nnext mutation round owns it."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"verification","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Verification"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"182b99262"},{"type":"text","value":", with the built "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dist"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/db"},{"type":"text","value":" Vitest, typecheck off: 200 files, 7,857 tests.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tsc --noEmit"},{"type":"text","value":": no errors."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pnpm --filter @tanstack/db test:dist"},{"type":"text","value":" (290 tests) and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pnpm test:minified-db"},{"type":"text","value":" pass."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Package unit tests: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"query-db-collection"},{"type":"text","value":" 558, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"electric-db-collection"},{"type":"text","value":" 629,\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"offline-transactions"},{"type":"text","value":" 242."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"insert-not-update-for-a-key-subscribers-saw-removed","text":"Insert, not update, for a key subscribers saw removed","level":1},{"id":"law","text":"Law","level":2},{"id":"gap","text":"Gap","level":2},{"id":"repair-and-witnesses","text":"Repair and witnesses","level":2},{"id":"limits","text":"Limits","level":2},{"id":"verification","text":"Verification","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"# Insert, not update, for a key subscribers saw removed\n\nPre-repair executable revision: `721a607e8` (oracle extension on `ef1e6a4aa`).\nRepair executable revision: `182b99262`.\n\n## Law\n\nEach change message must be valid for a consumer that has applied every\nearlier message: an insert names an absent key, and an update or delete names\na present one. Authority: the change-message contract in\n`packages/db/tests/change-event-history-oracle.test.ts` and issue #1901, which\nrequire a consumer that applies every message to agree with the Collection.\n\n## Gap\n\nWhen a sync commit made a previously absent key visible, `state.ts` checked\nfor a completed optimistic request on that key. If one existed, it emitted an\n`update` whose `previousValue` was that request's value. Subscribers had last\nseen the key removed, usually by a completed optimistic delete, so they got an\nupdate for a row they did not hold.\n\nThe change-event oracle missed it because its mirror applied inserts and\nupdates with the same `Map#set`. The message type was never checked.\n\nA mutation round on the state stack found it. The mutant that limited this\nbranch to updates (E3) survived the whole suite. With a strict mirror, the\noracle's histories showed 78 invalid updates on `main` and none under E3.\n\n## Repair and witnesses\n\n- The oracle's mirror records each message that is invalid for its state, and\n  every history asserts that the list is empty. The deferred-sync lane already\n  compared exact per-key traces.\n- A previously absent key now always gets an `insert`. When a buffered delete\n  for the key is still batched, `composeBatchedChange` turns the pair into an\n  update, as before.\n- The completed-request map becomes a key set, the only part that\n  virtual-property derivation reads. The `state.ts` module is 194 minified and\n  39 gzip bytes smaller.\n\n| Run | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Owner on `721a607e8` (oracle only) | 26 of 378 fail, each on an update for a key the mirror lacks |\n| Owner on `182b99262` | 378 pass |\n| Mutant: the old update branch | the 26 failures above |\n| Mutant: no event for a previously absent key | 92 of 538 owner tests fail |\n\n## Limits\n\n- The strict mirror runs in the change-event oracle's local-only histories.\n  Other owners that build mirrors may still accept an update for an absent key.\n- Survivor: building the completed-key set empty changes no test result. The\n  set only feeds the fallback for previous `$synced`/`$origin` when the\n  pre-sync capture lacks the key. This repair keeps that use unchanged; the\n  next mutation round owns it.\n\n## Verification\n\nOn `182b99262`, with the built `dist`:\n\n- `packages/db` Vitest, typecheck off: 200 files, 7,857 tests.\n  `tsc --noEmit`: no errors.\n- `pnpm --filter @tanstack/db test:dist` (290 tests) and\n  `pnpm test:minified-db` pass.\n- Package unit tests: `query-db-collection` 558, `electric-db-collection` 629,\n  `offline-transactions` 242.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"# Insert, not update, for a key subscribers saw removed\n\nPre-repair executable revision: `721a607e8` (oracle extension on `ef1e6a4aa`).\nRepair executable revision: `182b99262`.\n\n## Law\n\nEach change message must be valid for a consumer that has applied every\nearlier message: an insert names an absent key, and an update or delete names\na present one. Authority: the change-message contract in\n`packages/db/tests/change-event-history-oracle.test.ts` and issue #1901, which\nrequire a consumer that applies every message to agree with the Collection.\n\n## Gap\n\nWhen a sync commit made a previously absent key visible, `state.ts` checked\nfor a completed optimistic request on that key. If one existed, it emitted an\n`update` whose `previousValue` was that request's value. Subscribers had last\nseen the key removed, usually by a completed optimistic delete, so they got an\nupdate for a row they did not hold.\n\nThe change-event oracle missed it because its mirror applied inserts and\nupdates with the same `Map#set`. The message type was never checked.\n\nA mutation round on the state stack found it. The mutant that limited this\nbranch to updates (E3) survived the whole suite. With a strict mirror, the\noracle's histories showed 78 invalid updates on `main` and none under E3.\n\n## Repair and witnesses\n\n- The oracle's mirror records each message that is invalid for its state, and\n  every history asserts that the list is empty. The deferred-sync lane already\n  compared exact per-key traces.\n- A previously absent key now always gets an `insert`. When a buffered delete\n  for the key is still batched, `composeBatchedChange` turns the pair into an\n  update, as before.\n- The completed-request map becomes a key set, the only part that\n  virtual-property derivation reads. The `state.ts` module is 194 minified and\n  39 gzip bytes smaller.\n\n| Run | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Owner on `721a607e8` (oracle only) | 26 of 378 fail, each on an update for a key the mirror lacks |\n| Owner on `182b99262` | 378 pass |\n| Mutant: the old update branch | the 26 failures above |\n| Mutant: no event for a previously absent key | 92 of 538 owner tests fail |\n\n## Limits\n\n- The strict mirror runs in the change-event oracle's local-only histories.\n  Other owners that build mirrors may still accept an update for an absent key.\n- Survivor: building the completed-key set empty changes no test result. The\n  set only feeds the fallback for previous `$synced`/`$origin` when the\n  pre-sync capture lacks the key. This repair keeps that use unchanged; the\n  next mutation round owns it.\n\n## Verification\n\nOn `182b99262`, with the built `dist`:\n\n- `packages/db` Vitest, typecheck off: 200 files, 7,857 tests.\n  `tsc --noEmit`: no errors.\n- `pnpm --filter @tanstack/db test:dist` (290 tests) and\n  `pnpm test:minified-db` pass.\n- Package unit tests: `query-db-collection` 558, `electric-db-collection` 629,\n  `offline-transactions` 242.\n"}
